+++ b/xtask/src/process_bump_tests.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+//! Tests for `process_bump` (#1153): the bump is +1, one integer only, and the file is rewritten whole.
+
+use crate::process_bump::{bumped, run};
+
+#[test]
+fn bump_adds_one_and_ends_with_a_newline() {
+    assert_eq!(bumped("62\n").as_deref(), Ok("63\n"));
+    assert_eq!(bumped("  9 \r\n").as_deref(), Ok("10\n"));
+    assert_eq!(bumped("\u{feff}0").as_deref(), Ok("1\n"));
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn bump_refuses_anything_but_one_integer() {
+    for bad in ["", "abc", "62 63", "-1", "6.2"] {
+        assert!(bumped(bad).is_err(), "{bad:?} must be refused");
+    }
+    assert!(bumped(&u64::MAX.to_string()).is_err());
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn run_rewrites_the_file_and_refuses_arguments() {
+    let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("camcraft-process-bump-{}", std::process::id()));
+    let claude = dir.join(".claude");
+    std::fs::create_dir_all(&claude).expect("temp dir");
+    std::fs::write(claude.join("PROCESS_VERSION"), "41\n").expect("seed");
+    assert_eq!(run(&dir, &[]), Ok(0));
+    assert_eq!(std::fs::read_to_string(claude.join("PROCESS_VERSION")).expect("read"), "42\n");
+    assert!(run(&dir, &["--x".into()]).is_err());
+    let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir);
+}

From 9b79a44b61a1a6e06991af2dfe0c6db2ec846a98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:32:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(2d): trochoidal method for 2D Adaptive, confined to
 its region

2D Adaptive gains a Method: Spiral (the default - the HSM plan the kind
always ran, byte for byte, same stamp) or Trochoidal. The trochoidal
method cuts one lane of trochoid loops along the medial line of the
cutter-centre area (the region eroded by the tool radius and the stock
to leave), its loop band the least clearance along that line, planned by
the Trochoidal slot's measured-engagement ladder. The finished path is
then checked move by move against the area; a point outside refuses the
operation by name. A band wider than the tool gets an opened bore (a
helix at half the tool radius, then a two-centre semicircle spiral out
to the band) so no post is left at the lane's start.

Refused by name: a region narrower than the tool, too narrow to loop in,
a ring round an island, a region with no single medial line, a lane that
would leave more than 25 % of the region out of reach, a loop outside
the region, a drop past the helix turn cap, the Adaptive doors.

The method is an EditOperationParams edit, the `method` word of
`adaptive2_d` in the project file (absent reads as spiral) and so an MCP
`edit_operation` parameter, and a combo on the Passes tab.

Refs #1509

